# On the Educational Uses of Computer-Generated Cartoon Faces.

**Authors:** Pickover, Clifford A.

## Abstract
Focuses on use of computer-drawn faces to explore visualization in learning and for presenting multivariate data. Prior and new research are reviewed and future applications are discussed. "Autocorrelation-face," a graphics representation created from mathematical analysis of voice input, and its potential as a learning aid for the deaf are discussed. (MBR)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ315631

